   "updated": "Jun 30, 2023",
   "downloads": 89,
   "repo": "https://github.com/nickanderson/cfengine-delete-files",
   "documentation": null,
   "website": null,
   "commit": "84cce7c5653b6a5f2b5a28ebb33c697ffc676dd4",
   "discussion": "https://github.com/cfengine/core/discussions/new?category=modules&title=delete-files&body=I+have+a+question+regarding...",
   "discussionSearch": "https://github.com/cfengine/core/discussions/categories/modules?discussions_q=is%3Aopen+category%3AModules+delete-files",
   "version": "2.0.0",
   "readme": "\n<p>A simple module to delete specific files.</p>\n<p>\nIt allows you to specify a list of files you want deleted on hosts in your infrastructure. When this module is deployed as part of your policy set, every time CFEngine runs, it will check if those files exist, and delete them if they do.</p>\n<p>\n<strong>Recommendation:</strong> Enforce the removal of files known to be malicious or indicating insecure configuration.\nExamples of such files are `~/.shosts` files, `/etc/cron.deny`, etc.</p>\n<div id=\"outline-container-headline-1\" class=\"outline-2\">\n<h2 id=\"headline-1\">\nConfiguration\n</h2>\n<div id=\"outline-text-headline-1\" class=\"outline-text-2\">\n<div id=\"outline-container-headline-2\" class=\"outline-3\">\n<h3 id=\"headline-2\">\nModule input\n</h3>\n<div id=\"outline-text-headline-2\" class=\"outline-text-3\">\n<p>\nThis module accepts input.\nBoth the cfbs CLI and Mission Portal (3.21 and beyond) allow you to specify the files you want deleted.\nHere is an example of what it looks like in Mission Portal:</p>\n<p>\n<img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/nickanderson/cfengine-delete-files/main/delete-files-example-input-mp.png\" alt=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/nickanderson/cfengine-delete-files/main/delete-files-example-input-mp.png\" title=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/nickanderson/cfengine-delete-files/main/delete-files-example-input-mp.png\"></p>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"outline-container-headline-3\" class=\"outline-3\">\n<h3 id=\"headline-3\">\nVariables\n</h3>\n<div id=\"outline-text-headline-3\" class=\"outline-text-3\">\n<dl>\n<dt>\n<code class=\"verbatim\">delete_files:delete_files.files</code>\n</dt>\n<dd>\n<p>Array of dicts having <code class=\"verbatim\">path</code> and <code class=\"verbatim\">why</code> keys.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code class=\"verbatim\">path</code> must be a regular expression matching the fully qualified path to a file</li>\n<li><code class=\"verbatim\">why</code>  should explain why the file being absent is important</li>\n</ul>\n<figure>\n<div class=\"src src-json\">\n<div class=\"highlight\"><pre tabindex=\"0\" class=\"chroma\"><code class=\"language-json\" data-lang=\"json\"><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\">   <span class=\"p\">{</span>\n</span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\">     <span class=\"nt\">\"variables\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"p\">{</span>\n</span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\">       <span class=\"nt\">\"delete_files:delete_files.files\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"p\">{</span>\n</span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\">         <span class=\"nt\">\"comment\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"Files and their required permissions\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n</span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\">         <span class=\"nt\">\"value\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"p\">[</span>\n</span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\">           <span class=\"p\">{</span>\n</span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\">             <span class=\"nt\">\"why\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"The file lists remote hosts and users that are trusted by the local system when using the rshd daemon and can allow unauthenticated access to the system. Reccomended by CIS  CCE-84145-2.\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n</span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\">             <span class=\"nt\">\"path\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"/etc/hosts.equiv\"</span>\n</span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\">           <span class=\"p\">},</span>\n</span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\">           <span class=\"p\">{</span>\n</span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\">             <span class=\"nt\">\"why\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"The file lists remote hosts and users that are trusted by the local system when using the rshd daemon and can allow unauthenticated access to the system. Reccomended by CIS  CCE-84145-2.\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n</span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\">             <span class=\"nt\">\"path\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"/home/.*/.rhosts\"</span>\n</span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\">           <span class=\"p\">},</span>\n</span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\">           <span class=\"p\">{</span>\n</span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\">             <span class=\"nt\">\"why\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"The file lists remote hosts and users that are trusted by the local system when using the rshd daemon and can allow unauthenticated access to the system. Reccomended by CIS  CCE-84145-2.\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n</span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\">             <span class=\"nt\">\"path\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"/root/.rhosts\"</span>\n</span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\">           <span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\">         <span class=\"p\">]</span>\n</span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\">       <span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\">     <span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\">   <span class=\"p\">}</span></span></span></code></pre></div>\n</div>\n<figcaption>\nExample Augments configuration\n</figcaption>\n</figure>\n<p>\n<strong>Notes:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Running with class <code class=\"verbatim\">delete_files:DEBUG</code> or <code class=\"verbatim\">default:DEBUG</code> define results in DEBUG reports from policy.</li>\n<li>A list or array of files is also supported.</li>\n<li>An array with filenames and dicts having <code class=\"verbatim\">path</code>  and <code class=\"verbatim\">why</code> keys is supported.</li>\n<li>Absence of <code class=\"verbatim\">why</code> key is supported.</li>\n<li>A simple string is supported (but as indicated by DEBUG reports, likely a mis-configuration).</li>\n<li>Directories are <strong>not</strong> deleted.</li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"outline-container-headline-4\" class=\"outline-2\">\n<h2 id=\"headline-4\">\nHistory\n</h2>\n<div id=\"outline-text-headline-4\" class=\"outline-text-2\">\n<ul>\n<li>DEBUG reports added in version 2.0.0.</li>\n<li>Support for simple list specification added in version 2.0.0.</li>\n<li>Support for mixed data array specification added in version 2.0.0.</li>\n<li>Support for absence of <code class=\"verbatim\">why</code> key added in version 2.0.0.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</div>\n"
  }
 },
